00:23:02.620 --> 00:23:07.480
It's high noon, Sicily, and we're now three days into the borough of Arrowhead County's physician strike.

00:23:07.720 --> 00:23:12.830
And one day away from winter solstice, which means a full 24 hours of glorious darkness.

00:23:13.610 --> 00:23:19.820
And turning to the art scene, it seems my brother Chris has taken off headlong into a new creative direction.

00:23:20.180 --> 00:23:24.720
I'm not sure which particular muse has seized him, but clearly her grip is strong.

00:23:25.600 --> 00:23:29.980
And right now I'd like to turn the microphone over to Maurice Minifield, the president and general manager.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:31.940
of the Minifield Communications Network.

00:23:32.320 --> 00:23:32.560
Maurice?

00:23:35.960 --> 00:23:36.380
Thank you.

00:23:37.200 --> 00:23:38.080
I'll be brief.

00:23:39.170 --> 00:23:41.550
I'm collecting for a comrade-in-arms

00:23:41.550 --> 00:23:42.610
who's down on his luck.

00:23:42.750 --> 00:23:44.730
We need clean, serviceable clothes,

00:23:45.070 --> 00:23:47.310
canned goods, toiletries, that sort of thing.

00:23:47.940 --> 00:23:49.040
Bring him by the station.

00:23:49.080 --> 00:23:50.180
We'll make sure he gets them.

00:23:50.590 --> 00:23:53.200
Oh, and remember, this is not to dump.

00:23:53.680 --> 00:23:55.180
No rags, no junk,

00:23:55.380 --> 00:23:57.820
no three-year-old jars of pickled beets.

00:23:58.900 --> 00:23:59.560
Appreciate it.

00:24:02.060 --> 00:24:05.470
Excuse me. You okay in here?

00:24:06.290 --> 00:24:08.270
Yeah, fine. Uh, you work here?

00:24:08.610 --> 00:24:08.890
Yeah.

00:24:09.580 --> 00:24:13.520
You know, for a few cents more, you can get name-brand paper towels,

00:24:13.580 --> 00:24:16.700
which are a lot more absorbent than this, uh, institutional grade.

00:24:17.060 --> 00:24:18.420
I'll tell the boss soon as he wakes up.

00:24:18.860 --> 00:24:19.260
Do that.

00:24:20.140 --> 00:24:21.320
What? You...

00:24:30.670 --> 00:24:31.310
I need this, Dave.

00:24:31.590 --> 00:24:32.170
Okay by me?

00:24:33.660 --> 00:24:34.550
Hey, Chris.

00:24:34.750 --> 00:24:34.910
Dave.

00:24:35.480 --> 00:24:36.180
Hello, son.

00:24:40.390 --> 00:24:41.650
Cup of Joe, Dr. Fleischman?

00:24:42.900 --> 00:24:43.960
Shelly, let me ask you something.

00:24:44.830 --> 00:24:47.500
No, I thought that we were friends, that you liked me.

00:24:47.880 --> 00:24:48.320
I do.

00:24:48.740 --> 00:24:51.020
How is it that you can be a part of this lawsuit?

00:24:51.940 --> 00:24:52.380
Oh, that.

00:24:52.910 --> 00:24:54.050
Just being a team player.

00:24:54.270 --> 00:24:56.170
You know, all for one, one for all.

00:24:56.430 --> 00:24:58.530
Shelly, I'm going to snag me some of these bulbs.

00:24:59.270 --> 00:24:59.630
Okay.

00:25:00.220 --> 00:25:03.500
Hello, Joel. I'll have one of those.

00:25:03.900 --> 00:25:04.700
Okey-dokey.

00:25:05.080 --> 00:25:08.240
How can you look me in the eye and greet me as if nothing is different?

00:25:08.460 --> 00:25:09.640
As if nothing has changed?

00:25:09.960 --> 00:25:10.580
What do you mean?

00:25:10.820 --> 00:25:11.640
He means a lawsuit.

00:25:12.500 --> 00:25:13.040
Oh, that.

00:25:13.560 --> 00:25:14.340
Oh, that?

00:25:15.200 --> 00:25:16.000
Oh, that?

00:25:16.120 --> 00:25:18.700
This is incredible.

00:25:19.480 --> 00:25:21.020
What is wrong with you people?

00:25:21.200 --> 00:25:22.700
Don't you realize what you're doing?

00:25:22.920 --> 00:25:28.470
To me, your physician, I'm the guy who sets your broken bones, lowers your blood pressure,

00:25:28.770 --> 00:25:29.970
tramps out into the tundra in the...

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:31.520
in the middle of the night to deliver your babies.

00:25:31.780 --> 00:25:33.760
Every single one of you has stood before me naked,

00:25:33.940 --> 00:25:35.340
sick and needy, desperate for my health.

00:25:36.460 --> 00:25:38.520
Instead of gratitude, what do I get? What's my reward?

00:25:38.620 --> 00:25:40.620
How do you repay me? With malice and venom.

00:25:41.480 --> 00:25:43.360
I wouldn't take it too personally, Jerome.

00:25:46.720 --> 00:25:48.720
Have you ever heard of U.S. versus Hilligus?

00:25:48.920 --> 00:25:50.410
No. Let's see.

00:25:50.950 --> 00:25:52.650
Preble damages are upheld.

00:25:53.260 --> 00:25:54.500
Breaching scholarship agreement.

00:25:54.660 --> 00:25:56.540
United States Court of Appeals, Ninth Circuit.

00:25:57.180 --> 00:25:57.660
What do you think?

00:25:58.280 --> 00:25:59.980
Hilligus got an NHSC...

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:05.280
in exchange for agreeing to serve in a health manpower shortage area.

00:26:05.840 --> 00:26:08.180
After graduation, he tried to back out.

00:26:08.460 --> 00:26:11.030
The government sued him and won.

00:26:12.380 --> 00:26:15.200
This is exactly the kind of precedent we were looking for.

00:26:15.560 --> 00:26:15.900
Really?

00:26:16.560 --> 00:26:18.860
Maggie, I knew we had an excellent case against Joel,

00:26:18.960 --> 00:26:21.580
but now we have got him by the short hairs.

00:26:22.110 --> 00:26:22.850
That's wonderful.

00:26:23.310 --> 00:26:24.150
Don't get me wrong.

00:26:24.830 --> 00:26:27.630
You know, I mean, I sympathize with Joel's predicament. I do.

00:26:27.920 --> 00:26:29.980
But I gotta tell you, there is nothing...

00:26:30.030 --> 00:26:40.340
Nothing more satisfying in law than knowing that you are going to walk into that courtroom and grind your opponent's face into the marble floor.

00:26:41.170 --> 00:26:42.010
I can imagine.

00:26:42.670 --> 00:26:48.720
And you, you did it, Maggie. You put the final nail in Joel's coffin.

00:26:50.150 --> 00:26:50.650
Thank you.

00:26:51.550 --> 00:26:52.070
You're welcome.

00:26:57.090 --> 00:26:57.290
Guess?

00:26:59.330 --> 00:26:59.970
Guess I should...

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:02.220
Girl, I finished transcribing those depositions, huh?

00:27:03.010 --> 00:27:03.190
Okay.

00:27:04.520 --> 00:27:05.540
Yeah, right.

00:27:06.120 --> 00:27:06.960
Okay, bye.

00:27:18.610 --> 00:27:20.660
Hey, Ed, how's it going?

00:27:20.940 --> 00:27:22.380
Oh, good afternoon, Dr. Flashman.

00:27:22.910 --> 00:27:24.530
Say, could you hand me that other screwdriver?

00:27:25.990 --> 00:27:29.090
Boy, I'll tell you, these last few days have been a real eye-opener.

00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:30.680
I can imagine.

00:27:31.220 --> 00:27:34.220
I've seen up close and personal the dark underbelly of this town,

00:27:34.380 --> 00:27:35.720
and it is not a pretty sight.

00:27:37.180 --> 00:27:38.900
One thing for sure, you find out who your friends are.

00:27:40.140 --> 00:27:41.560
I won't forget it. I mean it.

00:27:41.560 --> 00:27:42.900
I won't forget how you stuck behind me.

00:27:43.460 --> 00:27:45.540
And all the others, Maurice, Ruthann, Mike,

00:27:46.060 --> 00:27:47.640
they couldn't wait to stab me in the back.

00:27:48.440 --> 00:27:50.300
But not you. You are a real mensch.

00:27:51.440 --> 00:27:52.580
Thank you, Dr. Fleischman.

00:27:56.440 --> 00:27:56.960
What's going on here?

00:27:57.660 --> 00:27:59.980
Oh, uh, I just finished changing...

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:02.260
the lock. What? Why? Well,

00:28:02.890 --> 00:28:04.810
the way Maurice put it is, as long as

00:28:04.810 --> 00:28:06.750
you refuse to provide medical services to the

00:28:06.750 --> 00:28:09.320
community, the community will refuse

00:28:09.320 --> 00:28:11.320
to provide you with lodging. What are you talking

00:28:11.320 --> 00:28:14.100
about? What about my stuff? Your stuff

00:28:14.100 --> 00:28:16.380
has been seized. Seized?

00:28:17.190 --> 00:28:19.190
Maurice says it's standard procedure in cases

00:28:19.190 --> 00:28:20.930
like this. Seized?

00:28:21.210 --> 00:28:23.310
Well, don't tell anyone, Dr. Fleischman, but

00:28:25.570 --> 00:28:27.730
packed you a spare change of underwear and a toothbrush.

00:28:32.590 --> 00:28:37.210
You know, Dr. Fleischman, I always thought your story would have a happy ending to Sir With Love.

00:28:38.040 --> 00:28:38.280
What?

00:28:39.000 --> 00:28:42.650
Well, Sidney Poitier takes this job working in the inner-city school,

00:28:42.810 --> 00:28:44.650
and at first he just hates being there.

00:28:45.060 --> 00:28:49.580
But then later, he comes to know his students and to really care about them deeply.

00:28:50.260 --> 00:28:54.690
And then at the end of the movie, he's offered this job, teaching at a very prestigious school,

00:28:55.110 --> 00:28:57.150
but he decides to stay right where he's at.

00:28:58.490 --> 00:28:59.870
But I guess that's just a movie, Hunter.

00:29:02.630 --> 00:29:15.740
Hey, Bristol, Bristol.

00:29:15.880 --> 00:29:16.220
Yeah.

00:29:16.560 --> 00:29:17.040
You in there?

00:29:17.180 --> 00:29:17.460
Yeah.

00:29:17.720 --> 00:29:18.240
Come out here.

00:29:18.620 --> 00:29:19.360
Got something for you.

00:29:20.330 --> 00:29:21.610
Thought you might could use this.

00:29:21.730 --> 00:29:25.310
There's some thermal underwear, bib overalls, some dental powder.

00:29:25.610 --> 00:29:26.750
Some food in there, too.

00:29:26.870 --> 00:29:28.930
Chicken noodle soup, creamed corn.

00:29:30.160 --> 00:29:31.900
Some clown threw in a jar of poi.

00:29:32.080 --> 00:29:33.140
You can use that if you want to.

00:29:34.490 --> 00:29:36.470
A couple of boxes just like that over at the station.

00:29:37.080 --> 00:29:37.620
What's this?

00:29:38.000 --> 00:29:39.540
Oh, those are shiitake mushrooms.

00:29:39.860 --> 00:29:40.840
You have to soak them.

00:29:41.430 --> 00:29:45.440
They had a nice musky flavor to stews, casserole.

00:29:45.640 --> 00:29:46.760
Yeah, that's lovely.

00:29:50.290 --> 00:29:52.290
Bristol, tell me something.

00:29:53.630 --> 00:29:54.290
How'd it happen?

00:29:55.120 --> 00:29:56.520
How'd you come to this sorry state?

00:29:57.450 --> 00:29:59.670
Was it, uh, drugs?

00:30:00.510 --> 00:30:03.330
I can understand, I mean, that no-win war, the temptation.

00:30:03.890 --> 00:30:05.210
No, I never did drugs.

00:30:05.800 --> 00:30:08.220
Was it that post-trauma rigmarole?

00:30:08.320 --> 00:30:08.620
No.

00:30:09.960 --> 00:30:12.620
Well, was it the erosion of our industrial base?

00:30:12.780 --> 00:30:14.320
The factory you work for closed down?

00:30:14.940 --> 00:30:16.780
I had a good job, cable TV company.

00:30:17.750 --> 00:30:19.460
Hmm, what happened then?

00:30:21.480 --> 00:30:22.380
Change of venue.

00:30:22.970 --> 00:30:23.130
Huh?

00:30:24.450 --> 00:30:27.290
It happened five years ago, summer, August.

00:30:28.670 --> 00:30:29.470
I was...

00:30:30.120 --> 00:30:34.480
Troubleshooting along a back road near this little farm town, Illinois, Watsika.

00:30:36.510 --> 00:30:44.080
Ten o'clock at night, I was up the power pole, and these lights came out of nowhere.

00:30:44.980 --> 00:30:45.480
White?

00:30:45.920 --> 00:30:47.600
Yeah, real bright.

00:30:47.820 --> 00:30:50.480
White, blue, green.

00:30:52.350 --> 00:30:59.250
And they came close, hovering over the cornfield, not making a sound, just watching me.

00:31:01.280 --> 00:31:09.960
and then they took off straight up fast it was a clear night but in a couple of

00:31:09.960 --> 00:31:22.440
seconds they were out of my sight they were gone well that time keeping my

00:31:22.440 --> 00:31:29.820
mind on things on work and girls Sunday afternoon football games

00:31:31.560 --> 00:31:33.700
No, the world had turned over.

00:31:39.610 --> 00:31:40.650
Change of venue.

00:31:40.950 --> 00:31:42.810
Yeah, exactly.

00:31:57.140 --> 00:31:58.340
Hey, did I wake you? I'm sorry.

00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:02.530
I used to have a lava lamp.

00:32:03.410 --> 00:32:04.650
Chris, it's three in the morning.

00:32:05.320 --> 00:32:05.900
It is?

00:32:06.420 --> 00:32:07.980
Yeah, I almost shot you.

00:32:08.540 --> 00:32:10.700
You still have that lava lamp? I think it was green.

00:32:11.700 --> 00:32:12.860
Yeah, I think it's in here somewhere.

00:32:14.130 --> 00:32:14.270
Yeah?

00:32:14.850 --> 00:32:16.270
The cord's broken.

